{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "fc", "rep": 205, "hyps": [{"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Raising an already large learning rate makes Adam diverge, causing large accuracy drops (exps 4, 5, 7, 13)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At tiny learning rates the network is undertrained, so a step up gives consistent gains (exps 1, 14)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deeper nets are less stable at high learning rates, so adding a layer then causes collapse (exps 85, 87)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "With slow learning, the extra capacity of a deeper net helps it fit more within the epoch budget (exps 84, 86)."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Raising an already strong L2 penalty pushes the model into underfitting (exps 64, 67, 71)."}, {"edit_param": "batch_size", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Larger batches reduce gradient noise and stabilize training at high learning rates (exp 48)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "batch_size", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "lower", "why": "Small, noisy batches combined with many updates amplify the instability of a higher learning rate (exp 7)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "depth", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Three-layer nets are the most sensitive to learning-rate increases (exps 12, 13)."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param